{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{9}) & =0 \\\\ -27{x}^{2}-12 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283199 13194139534283 true] [17592186283198 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534283 true] [17592186283198 1041 "field-1" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283198 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283199 13194139534283 true] [17592186283198 1110 #uuid "86178329-4413-5d1c-ba52-5856887faf1b" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283199 1034 "-27x^2-12" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283199 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534283 true] [17592186283199 1111 #uuid "02281ad3-91b7-507b-9153-43626a0c50bd" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283200 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283201 13194139534283 true] [17592186283200 1089 "q-281311" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283200 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534283 true] [17592186283200 1100 "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x=8\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $1,$ find the equation. Write your answer in the form $a{x}^{2}+bx+c=0,$ where $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are real constants.\n\n{{field-1}}$=0$" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283200 1113 #uuid "1134a1f2-209a-573b-ac08-b8c5a5fffa78" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283200 1145 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and $x=8\\text{i}$ is a root, its conjugate $x=-8\\text{i}$ must also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-8\\text{i})(x+8\\text{i})=0\n$$\n\nMultiplying out the parentheses and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{(8\\text{i})}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-64(-1) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+64 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283202 13194139534283 true] [17592186283201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283203 13194139534283 true] [17592186283201 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534283 true] [17592186283201 1041 "field-1" 13194139534283 true] [17