his gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16({x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{8}) & =0 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}+6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283206 13194139534283 true] [17592186283205 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534283 true] [17592186283205 1041 "field-1" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283205 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283206 13194139534283 true] [17592186283205 1110 #uuid "4b3a74b5-9d90-5552-a50a-10d2905522ae" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283206 1034 "16x^2+6" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283206 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534283 true] [17592186283206 1111 #uuid "ce23700a-2b77-5133-acc6-f6534c983e97" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283207 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283208 13194139534283 true] [17592186283207 1089 "q-281348" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283207 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534283 true] [17592186283207 1100 "A quadratic equation with real coefficients has a complex root $x=-2+\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $1,$ find the equation. Write your answer in the form $a{x}^{2}+bx+c=0,$ where $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are real constants.\n\n{{field-1}}$=0$" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283207 1113 #uuid "d5a28fcf-c3ae-5a1c-a194-46d9199c5b82" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283207 1145 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and $x=-2+\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}$ is a root, we know that its complex conjugate $x=-2-\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}$ is also a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-(-2+\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}))=0\n$$\n\nBy expanding the parentheses, we can write the equation in standard form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x(-2+\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i})-x(-2-\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i})+(-2+\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i})(-2-\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-\\cancel{x\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}}+2x+\\cancel{x\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}}+4-7{\\text{i}}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+4x+4+7 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+4x+11 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283208 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283209 13194139534283 true] [17592186283208 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534283 true] [17592186283208 1041 "field-1" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283208 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283209 13194139534283 true] [17592186283208 1110 #uuid "17a475e4-c705-56a4-a110-996e8c3ddbe6" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283209 1034 "x^2+4x+11" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283209 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534283 true] [17592186283209 1111 #uuid "28b24ede-2838-5c6b-adbf-6936e5d1c590" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283210 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283211 13194139534283 true] [17592186283210 1089 "q-28273" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283210 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534283 true] [17592186283210 1100 "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x=-1+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $4$, find the equation." 13194139534283 true] [17592186283210 1113 #uuid "1e697c3b-76f6-5723-8d77-8a32e3c28a88" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283210 1145 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and $x=-1+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}$ is a root, its conjugate $x=-1-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}$ must also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-(-1+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}))=0\n$$\n\nBy expanding the parentheses, we can write the equation in standard form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x(-1-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})-x(-1+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})+(-1-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})(-1+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+x+\\sqrt{3}x\\text{i}+x-\\sqrt{3}x\\text{i}+1-3{\\text{i}}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+1+3 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has roots $x=-1\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i},$ but the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $4.$ Therefore, to find the desired equation, we multiply the equation above by $4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}^{2}+2x+4) & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+8x+16 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283211 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283212 13194139534283 true] [17592186283211 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283213 13194139534283 true] [17592186283211 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283214 13194139534283 true] [17592186283211 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283215 13194139534283 true] [17592186283211 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283216 13194139534283 true] [17592186283211 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534283 true] [17592186283211 1041 "selection" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283211 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283213 13194139534283 true] [17592186283211 1110 #uuid "a2f8ab07-7280-509c-ad61-e921431e20e5" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283212 1034 "4{x}^{2}-2x-16=0" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283212 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534283 true] [17592186283212 1111 #uuid "376f4213-4af5-57dd-b9f8-73a4e2a4d3ee" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283213 1034 "4{x}^{2}+8x+16=0" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283213 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534283 true] [17592186283213 1111 #uuid "67b76494-66ed-5da4-9641-d4fe09e80ce1" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283214 1034 "4{x}^{2}-2x+4=0" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283214 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534283 true] [17592186283214 1111 #uuid "78701929-42a9-55ce-814e-5afaddace5fc" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283215 1034 "4{x}^{2}+16x-8=0" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534283 true] [17592186283215 1111 #uuid "7a5a5c6a-9401-574c-87ec-9f4443f335b7" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283216 1034 "4{x}^{2}-16x-8=0" 13194139534283 true] [17592186283216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534283 true] [17592186283216 1111 #uuid "b8c734cc-5827-50bf-a344-6686af216bab" 13194139534283 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-274997" 17592186283197 "q-274997/field-1" 17592186283198 "q-274997/field-1/b44dfb9afe2534df3f2ded89d277a06ff03e6d4fbcae4cd634006b33dc6bb5f0" 17592186